:td {} "2 –  3 August 2024"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2157"} "Stade de France, Saint-Denis, France"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/2013815"} "91 from 73 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "This event was hampered by the absence of " [:a {:href "/athletes/130722"} "Elaine Thompson-Herah"] " (JAM), gold medalist in 2016-20, and by injuries to " [:a {:href "/athletes/114740"} "Shelly-Ann Fraser-Pryce"] ", her teammate, who started but withdrew from the semi-finals due to a hamstring injury. Tokyo bronze medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/130733"} "Shericka Jackson"] " won the Jamaican trials and was selected for the Jamaican team, but she had to withdraw through injury during the Games. In their absence, the focus was on American " [:a {:href "/athletes/150638"} "Sha’Carri Richardson"] ", Saint Lucia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/2505468"} "Julien Alfred"] ", Ivorian " [:a {:href "/athletes/129723"} "Marie-Josée Ta Lou-Smith"] ", and Great Britain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/130204"} "Dina Asher-Smith"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Asher-Smith did not make it to the final, finishing fifth in her semi-final heat, but the other three favorites made it through. " [:a {:href "/athletes/150629"} "Melissa Jefferson"] " (USA) won the first semi, while Alfred took semi two, defeating Richardson, who could not catch Alfred after a poor start. Jamaican teen " [:a {:href "/athletes/150179"} "Tia Clayton"] " won the final semi."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The final was held on a wet track just after a rainstorm, which affected the inside lanes more because of the stadium overhang. Alfred had a good start but Richardson had a dismal one, with a reaction time of 0.221 seconds, and was still seventh after 40m. Tia Clayton had a very good start and was second to Alfred after 20m but then faded away to finish seventh. " [:a {:href "/athletes/126373"} "Mujinga Kambundji"] " (SUI) also had a pretty good start and was still in second position at mid-race when Richardson passed her. Jefferson passed Kambudji for third place at 70-80m. That was the race between the two favorites, as Richardson never got closer to Alfred, who led the race from the start to the end."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Alfred’s gold was the first ever Olympic medal for the island nation of Saint Lucia. She would add to it a few days later with a silver in the 200 metres. Both Richardson and Jefferson would add to their medal chest with golds in the 4x100 relay."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Preliminary Round"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "2134"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/2505468"} "Julien Alfred"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/LCA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/LCA.png"}] "LCA"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "10.95 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "10.84 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "10.72 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "2466"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/150638"} "Sha'Carri Richardson"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "10.94 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "10.89 (2 h2)"] [:td {} "10.87 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "2444"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/150629"} "Melissa Jefferson"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td 